.DS_Store

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Browser state, media, logs live under $HOME/.config/agent-browser/
# and $HOME/.social-skills/. These entries are defensive in case anyone
# overrides paths into the repo.
profiles/
sessions/
media/
logs/

# Drafted long-form posts / articles — local only, not tracked.
articles/

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# --- Personal config (see PERSONAL.md) ---
# The repo is structured so all PII / brand-specific content lives in files
# that are gitignored here, with parallel `*.example` versions committed as
# templates. Copy from the example, fill in your handles/IDs, and the working
# files below are picked up automatically.

# Per-user brand config (handles, company id, content domain). Schema in
# config/brand.example.json — copy that to config/brand.json and edit.
config/brand.json

# Per-user Claude Code addendum — Claude Code auto-loads CLAUDE.local.md
# alongside CLAUDE.md (a symlink to AGENTS.md). Shape in CLAUDE.local.md.example.
CLAUDE.local.md
*.local.md
!*.local.md.example

# Wholly personal area: anything you don't want committed. Mirror of
# personal.example/ for things you've copied + customized but don't want
# to share back upstream.
personal/

# Brand-specific composite skills (drives an iOS app, captions are domain
# specific). Shared skills live in skills/; .claude/skills is a compatibility
# symlink for Claude Code. Copy templates to skills/post-daily-<your-domain>/
# and customize.
skills/post-daily-*/
.claude/skills/post-daily-*/

# Brand-specific cron entrypoints + ancillary helpers. Templates in
# personal.example/scripts/. Copy to scripts/ if you want them on disk
# under the same names your crontab uses.
scripts/daily_devotional.sh
scripts/daily_content.sh
scripts/devotional_video.sh
scripts/devotional_video_remote.sh
